---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const practices = [
  {
    title: 'Semantic structure',
    detail:
      'Real landmarks and a correct heading order on every page, so screen readers and assistive technology can navigate by structure rather than guessing from visual styling.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Keyboard operation',
    detail:
      'Every interactive control is reachable and operable by keyboard, with a visible focus indicator, and a skip link so keyboard users are not forced through the navigation on each page.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Contrast',
    detail:
      'Text and interface colours are checked against WCAG contrast ratios rather than chosen by eye. We publish the numbers for our own site below.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Text alternatives',
    detail:
      'Meaningful images carry descriptive alternative text; decorative images are marked as decorative so they are skipped rather than announced.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Motion preferences',
    detail:
      'Entrance animations are disabled for visitors whose system requests reduced motion, under the prefers-reduced-motion media query.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Works without JavaScript',
    detail:
      'Content is visible and readable with scripting unavailable. Animation and interactive enhancement layer on top rather than being required to read the page.',
  },
];

const ourSite = [
  { pair: 'Body text on white', ratio: '16.2:1' },
  { pair: 'Muted text on white', ratio: '8.3:1' },
  { pair: 'Crimson links and headings on white', ratio: '7.7:1' },
  { pair: 'Forest green on white', ratio: '8.1:1' },
  { pair: 'White on crimson buttons', ratio: '7.7:1' },
  { pair: 'White on the darkest hero green', ratio: '11.5:1' },
  { pair: 'White on the lightest hero green', ratio: '5.2:1' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility | Bee Balm Productions"
  description="How Bee Balm Productions approaches WCAG 2.1 AA and Section 508 conformance, and the measured contrast ratios for this site."
>
  <section class="container hero reveal">
    <div>
      <h1>Accessibility</h1>
      <p>
        Public bodies, health systems and federally funded programs are required to make their
        digital services accessible. We build to that standard by default rather than treating it as
        an add-on, because retrofitting it afterwards costs several times more than doing it first.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container curve-band">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <h2>The standards that apply</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <article class="panel reveal">
        <h3>WCAG 2.1 Level AA</h3>
        <p>
          The Web Content Accessibility Guidelines are the international reference standard. Level AA
          is what procurement almost always asks for, and what we target on client work.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel reveal">
        <h3>Section 508</h3>
        <p>
          Section 508 of the Rehabilitation Act governs federal agencies and organizations receiving
          federal funds. Since the 2017 refresh it incorporates WCAG 2.0 AA directly, so building to
          WCAG 2.1 AA satisfies it and goes slightly further.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel reveal">
        <h3>State and municipal policy</h3>
        <p>
          Many New Hampshire and Vermont public bodies apply the same requirements through their own
          procurement rules. We can supply conformance documentation as part of a bid.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container curve-band">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <h2>What we do on every build</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      {
        practices.map((item) => (
          <article class="value-card reveal">
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p>{item.detail}</p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container curve-band">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <h2>This site, measured</h2>
      <p>
        Published rather than claimed. These are the contrast ratios for this site's own palette,
        calculated against the WCAG formula. AA requires 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text.
      </p>
    </div>
    <article class="panel reveal">
      <table class="a11y-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Colour pair</th>
            <th scope="col">Contrast</th>
            <th scope="col">AA</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            ourSite.map((row) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{row.pair}</th>
                <td>{row.ratio}</td>
                <td>Pass</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="container curve-band">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <h2>Being straight about scope</h2>
    </div>
    <article class="panel reveal">
      <p>
        This site has not been through a third-party accessibility audit, and we do not claim a
        formal conformance certification for it. What is stated above is what has been built and
        measured, and the contrast figures can be checked against the published palette.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a project where conformance has to be demonstrated rather than described — a public
        procurement, a federally funded program — we will scope formal testing, including assistive
        technology testing, and produce an Accessibility Conformance Report. That is separate work
        with a real cost, and we would rather name it than imply it is already done.
      </p>
      <p>
        Found a problem on this site, or have trouble using any part of it? Email
        <a href="mailto:info@beebalmproductions.com">info@beebalmproductions.com</a> and we will fix it.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .a11y-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .a11y-table th,
  .a11y-table td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .a11y-table thead th {
    font-weight: 700;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .a11y-table tbody th {
    font-weight: 500;
  }
</style>
